I reviewed the full 31-slide Enterprise_Database_Services_Roadmap against the meeting transcript and the two worksheets in Enterprise_Database_Roadmap_Changes_FY27_FY28. The key issue is not just adding more initiatives. Several existing slides currently present unresolved directions, particularly DB2 retirement, NORTH ownership, engine placement, AI databases, and maturity targets, as if they are already approved decisions.

Recommended overall storyline

The deck should tell this story:

Why the database estate must change
What direction is already confirmed
What still requires a decision
Which capabilities must be established
Which modernization programs create demand
How the 2027–2028 roadmap will sequence decisions, enablement, and migrations

The main deck should stay executive-level. Put the detailed database decision matrix, service classifications, NFR tiers, and dependency register in the appendix.

